        <mxCell id="c46" value="&lt;i&gt;Both sets of effects add up to the same change, −$115,046, and volume is the same at both levels (+$7,886). The rest divides differently because the level differs: at the product-type level, shifts between items within a type appear as price and cost, not as mix. Every bar starts at the zero line.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="466" width="860" height="38" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
